WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.491
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.791 --> 00:00:16.145
Unit twenty-eight: Emotional Intelligence. In this unit, you will discuss emotions and reflect on past behaviour.

4
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.430
self-awareness.

5
00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:22.790
self-awareness means understanding your own feelings and behaviour.

6
00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.157
Self-awareness helps you improve your relationships.

7
00:00:26.857 --> 00:00:29.370
Your turn. Say: self-awareness.

8
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.489
self-awareness.

9
00:00:34.483 --> 00:00:35.984
emotional intelligence.

10
00:00:36.684 --> 00:00:40.994
emotional intelligence means the ability to understand and manage emotions.

11
00:00:41.294 --> 00:00:43.665
Good leaders have high emotional intelligence.

12
00:00:44.365 --> 00:00:47.133
Your turn. Say: emotional intelligence.

13
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:51.484
emotional intelligence.

14
00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:53.589
self-control.

15
00:00:54.289 --> 00:00:57.833
self-control means the ability to control your actions and feelings.

16
00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:00.817
It takes self-control not to shout when you're angry.

17
00:01:01.517 --> 00:01:04.053
Your turn. Say: self-control.

18
00:01:06.753 --> 00:01:07.987
self-control.

19
00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:10.217
social skills.

20
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:14.704
social skills means the ability to communicate well with others.

21
00:01:15.004 --> 00:01:18.060
Team sports help children develop social skills.

22
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.436
Your turn. Say: social skills.

23
00:01:24.136 --> 00:01:25.764
social skills.

24
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.076
conflict resolution.

25
00:01:28.776 --> 00:01:32.320
conflict resolution means ending a disagreement in a peaceful way.

26
00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.281
The course teaches conflict resolution at work.

27
00:01:35.981 --> 00:01:39.249
Your turn. Say: conflict resolution.

28
00:01:41.949 --> 00:01:43.554
conflict resolution.

29
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.911
burnout recovery.

30
00:01:46.611 --> 00:01:50.782
burnout recovery means the process of getting well after extreme work stress.

31
00:01:51.082 --> 00:01:53.476
Burnout recovery can take several months.

32
00:01:54.176 --> 00:01:56.828
Your turn. Say: burnout recovery.

33
00:01:59.528 --> 00:02:00.796
burnout recovery.

34
00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:02.692
gratitude.

35
00:02:03.392 --> 00:02:05.844
gratitude means the feeling of being thankful.

36
00:02:06.144 --> 00:02:08.968
Writing three things you're grateful for builds gratitude.

37
00:02:09.668 --> 00:02:12.332
Your turn. Say: gratitude.

38
00:02:15.032 --> 00:02:16.137
gratitude.

39
00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:18.186
vulnerability.

40
00:02:18.886 --> 00:02:22.244
vulnerability means being open about your feelings and weaknesses.

41
00:02:22.544 --> 00:02:24.880
Showing vulnerability can build trust.

42
00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.012
Your turn. Say: vulnerability.

43
00:02:30.712 --> 00:02:31.887
vulnerability.

44
00:02:32.883 --> 00:02:34.964
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:35.264 --> 00:02:38.706
I shouted at a colleague yesterday. I shouldn't have done that.

46
00:02:40.017 --> 00:02:40.844
What happened?

47
00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.754
I was exhausted. I ought to have taken a break before the meeting.

48
00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.759
Self-awareness is the first step. Did you apologise?

49
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.387
Yes. Showing some vulnerability actually helped.

50
00:02:56.683 --> 00:03:01.124
That's emotional intelligence. Conflict resolution starts with honesty.

51
00:03:02.417 --> 00:03:04.846
Grammar focus: should have / ought to have.

52
00:03:05.146 --> 00:03:08.469
Use should have or ought to have for things that were right but didn't happen.

53
00:03:08.769 --> 00:03:11.453
Use shouldn't have for things that were wrong but did happen.

54
00:03:11.753 --> 00:03:15.741
For example: I should have listened more carefully. I shouldn't have shouted.

55
00:03:16.041 --> 00:03:20.513
Use these forms to reflect on mistakes and to criticise past actions politely.

56
00:03:21.517 --> 00:03:24.111
Now read and listen. Why EQ Matters.

57
00:03:24.411 --> 00:03:28.674
For many years, people believed that intelligence was the key to success.

58
00:03:29.983 --> 00:03:33.806
Today, researchers say emotional intelligence is just as important.

59
00:03:35.117 --> 00:03:39.113
People with strong self-awareness and self-control handle stress better.

60
00:03:40.417 --> 00:03:44.018
Social skills and conflict resolution help teams work together.

61
00:03:45.317 --> 00:03:48.709
Many leaders admit they should have focused on these skills much earlier.

62
00:03:50.017 --> 00:03:52.332
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.818
The feeling of being thankful is blank.

64
00:03:55.118 --> 00:03:59.375
A, gratitude. B, vulnerability. C, self-control.

65
00:04:03.383 --> 00:04:05.244
The answer is A: gratitude.

66
00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.333
I failed the test. I blank studied more.

67
00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:13.193
A, should have. B, shouldn't have. C, must have.

68
00:04:17.183 --> 00:04:19.160
The answer is A: should have.

69
00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.302
You blank said that. It hurt her feelings.

70
00:04:23.602 --> 00:04:27.035
A, should have. B, shouldn't have. C, ought have.

71
00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.933
The answer is B: shouldn't have.

72
00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:36.705
Ending a disagreement peacefully is blank.

73
00:04:37.005 --> 00:04:41.947
A, conflict resolution. B, burnout recovery. C, social skills.

74
00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.635
The answer is A: conflict resolution.

75
00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:53.543
According to the text, what is just as important as intelligence?

76
00:04:53.843 --> 00:04:57.334
A, money. B, emotional intelligence. C, luck.

77
00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:04.011
The answer is B: emotional intelligence.

78
00:05:05.517 --> 00:05:09.864
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe a situation you would handle differently now.

79
00:05:15.164 --> 00:05:20.266
I once argued with a friend. I should have listened first and shouldn't have raised my voice.

80
00:05:20.566 --> 00:05:21.974
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:22.983 --> 00:05:26.808
Great work today! You learned eight new words and should have / ought to have.

82
00:05:27.108 --> 00:05:30.306
Today's value is empathy. Think about how others feel.

83
00:05:30.606 --> 00:05:33.456
See you in Unit twenty-nine. Goodbye!

84
00:05:33.756 --> 00:05:36.524
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

